; A `handle` whose body reaches an effect through a function value the
; walk cannot follow.
;
; `viaDirect` performs `Console` and names only `Alloc`, so AX3011
; refuses it - the body is KNOWN to reach an unhandled effect.
;
; `viaField` is the same program with one indirection: the same
; function, reached through a struct field. The walk cannot follow a
; word out of memory, so the body's effect set comes back a LOWER
; BOUND, and a handled-effects list cannot be checked against a lower
; bound. It used to be checked anyway, and silently passed.
;
; That silence was not a missing warning. An effect operation reached
; with no handler installed aborts the process with status 71 and no
; message, so the compile-time refusal became a runtime trap: this
; file without `viaDirect` built clean and died at 71.
;
; AX3038 informs rather than refuses, because it cannot know. Dispatch
; through a stored function is a legitimate program - `b.f` may well be
; pure - and refusing here would make the shape unwriteable rather than
; unverified. AX3011 keeps SEV_ERROR at every site where it fires.
(effect Console
  (log :: (-> String Int)))

(struct Box
  (f : (-> Int Int)))

(:: usesLog (-> Int Int))

(fn (usesLog n)
  {
    (log "op")
    n
  }
)

(:: install Box)

(fn (install) (Box usesLog))

(:: viaDirect (-> Int Int))

(fn (viaDirect n)
  (handle (usesLog n) (Alloc) (lambda (v) 0))
)

(:: viaField (-> Box Int))

(fn (viaField b)
  (handle (b.f 7) (Alloc) (lambda (v) 0))
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (+ (viaDirect 1) (viaField install)))
